; DOCS_warmStartDocumentLoader.loadModelChunk(DOCS_modelChunk); DOCS_modelChunk = undefined;</script><script nonce="fD3uVqZi3kyUUj8fu_36sA">DOCS_modelChunkParseStart = new Date().getTime();</script><script nonce="fD3uVqZi3kyUUj8fu_36sA">DOCS_modelChunk = [{"ty":"is","ibi":16088,"s":"d.\tProvides other information as necessary. \n3.\tThe FCOI Policy has been accepted by the PI or senior/key personnel \n\t________________________________________\n\tName of Responsible Official\t\n     \t ________________________________________\t_________________\n\tSignature of Responsible Official\t\t\t   \tDate\n\tRonin Institute for Independent Scholarship 2.0\n\nAppendix B: Management Plan Template\nThe Financial Conflict of Interest (FCOI) management plan template outlines procedures to mitigate or eliminate conflicts of interest that may arise in research settings. It\u0027s a crucial document for ensuring objectivity and integrity in research, particularly when funded by federal agencies like NIH.The plan details how to manage, reduce, or eliminate identified conflicts, focusing on safeguarding the research\u0027s objectivity. \nKey Elements of an FCOI Management Plan Template:\nInvestigator Information: Details of the investigator with the conflict, including name and role. \n\nEntity Information: Name of the entity with which the investigator has a conflict. \n\nNature of Conflict: Description of the financial interest (e.g., consulting fees, equity, travel) and its value (or estimated value). \n\nRelationship to Research: Explanation of how the financial interest relates to the research project and the basis for determining a conflict. \n\nManagement Plan Components:\nInvestigator\u0027s Role: Description of the investigator\u0027s specific duties in the research. \nConditions: Specific actions or restrictions imposed to manage the conflict. \nSafeguarding Objectivity: Explanation of how the plan will ensure objectivity in the research. \nAgreement: Confirmation that the investigator agrees to abide by the management plan. \n\nMonitoring and Reporting: Procedures for monitoring the plan\u0027s effectiveness and reporting on its status. \n\nAnnual Review: Requirement for periodic review and potential updates to the plan. \n\nExamples of Management Strategies:\nPublic Disclosure: Disclosing the conflict in publications, presentations, and to research participants.\nIndependent Review: Appointing an independent reviewer to oversee the research.\nModifying the Research Plan: Adjusting the research plan to minimize the conflict.\nPersonnel Changes: Reassigning roles or removing the investigator from the conflicted area.\nReducing or Eliminating the Conflict: This could involve selling equity or ending the relationship causing the conflict. \n\nImportance of the Management Plan:\nCompliance: Meets the requirements of federal agencies like the NIH.\nObjectivity: Ensures research remains unbiased and reliable.\nTransparency: Promotes openness and accountability in the research process.\nPublic Trust: Helps maintain public confidence in research findings\nAppendix C: Training Requirements Checklist\nDepending on the source of support for the relevant activities, more stringent training may be required, but the minimum training required for all persons affiliated with RIIS 2.0 is the online training specified by the National Institutes of Health\n\u000bAppendix D: Relevant Federal Regulations Reference\nFederal regulations\nThe primary federal regulation governing Financial Conflicts of Interest (FCOI) in research is 42 CFR Part 50 Subpart F, also known as the \"Promoting Objectivity in Research\" regulation. \nThis regulation establishes standards designed to ensure that the design, conduct, and reporting of research funded by the Public Health Service (PHS), which includes the National Institutes of Health (NIH), are free from bias due to an investigator\u0027s conflicting financial interests. \nKey aspects of the PHS FCOI regulations include:\nDisclosure of Financial Interests: Investigators are required to disclose their significant financial interests related to their institutional responsibilities, including compensation from non-profit entities and sponsored travel.\nDefinition of Significant Financial Interest (SFI): For PHS investigators, an SFI includes anything of monetary value over $5,000 received or held by the investigator, their spouse, or dependent children, that reasonably appears to be related to the investigator\u0027s institutional responsibilities.\n"},{"ty":"ae","et":"list","id":"kix.list.1","epm":{"le_nb":{"nl_4":{"b_gf":"%4","b_ts":{"ts_un":false,"ts_un_i":false,"ts_sc":false,"ts_it_i":true,"ts_fgc2":{"hclr_color":"#000000","clr_type":0},"ts_st_i":true,"ts_bgc2":{"hclr_color":null,"clr_type":0},"ts_fs_i":true,"ts_ff_i":true,"ts_bgc2_i":true,"ts_it":false,"ts_va":"nor","ts_bd_i":true,"ts_va_i":true,"ts_fs":11.0,"ts_ff":"Arial","ts_st":false,"ts_bd":false,"ts_fgc2_i":true,"ts_sc_i":true,"ts_tw":400},"b_ifl":162.0,"b_gs":"○","b_a":0,"b_sn":1,"b_gt":9,"b_il":180.0},"nl_3":{"b_gf":"%3","b_ts":{"ts_un":false,"ts_un_i":false,"ts_sc":false,"ts_it_i":true,"ts_fgc2":{"hclr_color":"#000000","clr_type":0},"ts_st_i":true,"ts_bgc2":{"hclr_color":null,"clr_type":0},"ts_fs_i":true,"ts_ff_i":true,"ts_bgc2_i":true,"ts_it":false,"ts_va":"nor","ts_bd_i":true,"ts_va_i":true,"ts_fs":11.0,"ts_ff":"Arial","ts_st":false,"ts_bd":false,"ts_fgc2_i":true,"ts_sc_i":true,"ts_tw":400},"b_ifl":126.0,"b_gs":"●","b_a":0,"b_sn":1,"b_gt":9,"b_il":144.0},"nl_2":{"b_gf":"%2","b_ts":{"ts_un":false,"ts_un_i":false,"ts_sc":false,"ts_it_i":true,"ts_fgc2":{"hclr_color":"#000000","clr_type":0},"ts_st_i":true,"ts_bgc2":{"hclr_color":null,"clr_type":0},"ts_fs_i":true,"ts_ff_i":true,"ts_bgc2_i":true,"ts_it":false,"ts_va":"nor","ts_bd_i":true,"ts_va_i":true,"ts_fs":11.0,"ts_ff":"Arial","ts_st":false,"ts_bd":false,"ts_fgc2_i":true,"ts_sc_i":true,"ts_tw":400},"b_ifl":90.0,"b_gs":"■","b_a":0,"b_sn":1,"b_gt":9,"b_il":108.0},"nl_1":{